> How about a special nethack Pacman level!

I don't think so.

Pacman is only interesting because it is a real time
game. Unlike Sokoban, another turn by turn game that
grafted fairly nicely into NetHack, Pacman would
always be an ugly fit.

And I doubt anyone would agree to turning NetHack
into a game where muscle twitch reflex use is the
most important thing even in a small part of the
game. For most of us, trying to _suppress_ twitch
reflexes, and think things through instead, is the
game's biggest challenge.

I can pretty much guarantee that stepping off a
Pacman level where doing things as fast as possible
was required, would be a death sentence on the next
level, where the play style inverted to "slow and
careful or die, die, die" mode again.

